From a2a0fc61aa54df17eef56e5705829192858607f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:16:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 71/91] Wormholes: Crucible statics, shared mass and lifetime,
 K162 on first warp

- every w-space system keeps its statics open (new mapWormholeSystems table, from
  pathfinder's static list).  C4 systems get the one static they had in Crucible;
  the second came with Hyperion.  A static that collapses comes back at once
- both ends of a wormhole share one mass and lifetime (new sysWormholes table).
  Each jump takes the ship's mass, prop module included.  It collapses when the
  mass or the time runs out, and the slim item shows the real size, age, expiry
  and the class of the system on the other side (it showed its own system's)
- the K162 and the destination are picked when the first ship warps to the
  wormhole, not when it spawns
- a pilot can jump through a wormhole twice in 4 minutes, must be within 5 km of
  it, and lands within 5 km of the far end (it was 2 km from the centre, inside
  the ball)
- wandering wormholes never use a type that is a static somewhere, and a new one
  turns up in the system 30-120 minutes after one collapses
- wormholes are only made when WormHoleEnabled is on
- /wormhole lists the wormholes in your system, spawns one by type, or collapses one
